          "id": "biology-plant-growth-2",
          "show": "",
          "say": "Auxin made at the shoot tip stimulates cell elongation and bends stems toward light while inhibiting side buds. Gibberellin promotes rapid stem elongation and bolting, while cytokinin, or kinin, stimulates cell division and bud growth.",
